       "minItems": 1,
-      "description": "What the renderer mounts for this scene (T-1739), and nothing it does not list. `terrain` and `water` are the epoch's own ground and water. `structures` is the structure records that resolve at target_date. The rest are the town's derived and authored layers, every one of them written for 1 July 1835 in a directory that carries no date: `flora` (the sward, the timber and the ground's substrate colours), `fauna`, `streets`, `enclosures` (with the ground inside them), `signage`, `yard_goods`, `frontage`, `wharves`, `boats`, `wells`, `residents` (the people directory), `businesses` (the firms register) and `exclusions` (the research record of buildings left out, and the watch list); tools/compile_scene.py compiles the people directory and the exclusions record only for a scene that lists them. The drawer follows the same list (T-1740): `residents` offers the People section and the City, Population and Order book topics, `businesses` the Firms section, `fauna` the wildlife topic, `flora` the plants topic and `exclusions` the not-here and open-questions topics, and a scene that does not list one offers none of what it carries. `street_grid` is a dated layer, data/street_grid/<scene>.json (T-0474, the 1904 Prairie Avenue carriageways, block faces, alleys and parcels). `context` is the faded context city (T-2477): data/context/<scene>.json, generated by tools/build_context_1904.py, simple stand-ins read off the Sanborn sheets and projected past them on every part of the map not yet built. `street_trees` is data/street_trees/<scene>.json (T-2473, the parkway elms planted on that grid's parkway bands). `railway` is a dated layer, data/railway/<scene>.json (T-2478, the 1904 Illinois Central tracks along the lake, their ballast, ties and verges). `humans` is the human figures (T-1788): data/humans/instances/<scene>/index.json and the instance records it names, each bound to a person in that scene's people directory and drawn only as data/humans/contract.json § l1 allows — while L1 is in force, nobody. A scene of another date lists only what is true of it."
+      "description": "What the renderer mounts for this scene (T-1739), and nothing it does not list. `terrain` and `water` are the epoch's own ground and water. `structures` is the structure records that resolve at target_date. The rest are the town's derived and authored layers, every one of them written for 1 July 1835 in a directory that carries no date: `flora` (the sward, the timber and the ground's substrate colours), `fauna`, `streets`, `enclosures` (with the ground inside them), `signage`, `yard_goods`, `frontage`, `wharves`, `boats`, `wells`, `residents` (the people directory), `businesses` (the firms register) and `exclusions` (the research record of buildings left out, and the watch list); tools/compile_scene.py compiles the people directory and the exclusions record only for a scene that lists them. The drawer follows the same list (T-1740): `residents` offers the People section and the City, Population and Order book topics, `businesses` the Firms section, `fauna` the wildlife topic, `flora` the plants topic and `exclusions` the not-here and open-questions topics, and a scene that does not list one offers none of what it carries. `street_grid` is a dated layer, data/street_grid/<scene>.json (T-0474, the 1904 Prairie Avenue carriageways, block faces, alleys and parcels). `context` is the faded context city (T-2477): data/context/<scene>.json, generated by tools/build_context_1904.py, simple stand-ins read off the Sanborn sheets and projected past them on every part of the map not yet built. `street_trees` is data/street_trees/<scene>.json (T-2473, the parkway elms planted on that grid's parkway bands). `railway` is a dated layer, data/railway/<scene>.json (T-2478, the 1904 Illinois Central tracks along the lake, their ballast, ties and verges). `humans` is the human figures (T-1788): data/humans/instances/<scene>/index.json and the instance records it names, each bound to a person in that scene's people directory and drawn only as data/humans/contract.json \u00a7 l1 allows \u2014 while L1 is in force, nobody. A scene of another date lists only what is true of it. `standing_horses` is a separate static skinned authored-development animal layer from data/transport/parked/standing-horses.json, explicitly scoped by scene, with reconstructed individual/appearance/size/placement and modern licensed asset attribution. It does not imply riding, tying, gait, hitching, driver or photographic-master acceptance."
