@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Licensed horse contact annotation / rigid support source review
+
+The finite source-frame/support mathematics is mechanically coherent for an additive standing-consumer proposal. This does not approve a final source freeze while the original contact metadata still says no pitch: preserve that original history, and explicitly supersede it in the final annotation with the later reconstructed whole-root support rotation. No build/browser or independent geometry decode ran in this review.
+
+Verified source41acd9bee7bf05fbcdd813fad965027b01b8801d6a21ca1c22eb2178c8842988 and decoder/contact/upright/reader hashes against actual files. Normalization is uniform metres-per-native-unit with translated source origin, Y-up/Z-forward/X-left; yawπ−heading maps canonical coordinates into ENU consistently. The declared withers proxy becomes1.55m canonically; it is an authored size choice, not measured breed/source scale. After support rotation its Y above root is1.547489497m, correctly disclosed separately.
+
+Independently reconstructed the quaternion matrix: maximum matrix difference8.67e−19, orthogonality error1.11e−16, quaternion norm1 within rounding. Rz(roll)*Rx(pitch) is consistent with the stated small0.396145° rigid tilt. A consumer must compose scene yaw outside this LOCAL support rotation, then source normalization, preserving the original skinned hierarchy/weights/bind matrices. The one linear fit only estimates angles; the subsequent exact rotation, ground resampling and maximum support-base correction are the controlling sampled placement. No per-foot offsets or geometry deformation are in that math.
+
+488 original lower-patch samples and474 equal10mm clipped-slab samples have internally matching stored arrays/extrema and no recorded penetration below−1µm. Maximum per-foot MINIMUM gap is0.1288567mm; this must not be restated as every surface sample being within that gap. Maximum selected-surface gaps are30.5463mm and10.9043mm respectively, because the definitions include raised underside/side geometry. This is finite sampled support, not continuous triangle/terrain contact, a contact-force model or anatomical sole certification. The original upright5.771mm result remains history.
+
+The63/63/7/6 triangle asymmetry and disconnected index-patch components reflect selection/tessellation/seam behavior; counts do not identify a complete anatomical hoof. The current exact surface IDs are annotations, not rig bones, certified sockets or historical evidence. Any welded connectivity check is supplemental and cannot establish anatomy or continuous contact. Actual normalized source views must confirm fore/hind/left/right assignment and scale, and actual consumer readback must bind source skin/normal/material/UV parity, composed transforms, samples and updated tilted bounds/clearance. Scene placement is reconstructed yard presence, not an attested named horse or breed.
+
+Runtime grounding should use the authoritative rendered yard-surface API. The investigative reader's hardcoded22mm lift must not silently become a second runtime ground policy. Preserve all original source/license provenance, source bytes and failed/nonqualifying predecessors; no previous synthetic horse rig or photograph claim transfers.
+
+No app/ticket/Git/network/build/browser or source-model mutation performed. Source checks are inSOURCE-CHECKS.json.
